{"id":"h4-03-q1","title":"Queues vs logs","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: SQS, RabbitMQ, Kafka, when each fits, consumer groups and ordering. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"why-queues-exist","title":"Why queues exist","html":"<p><strong>A queue lets a producer hand off work and move on, while a consumer processes it later at its own pace.</strong> It decouples two things in time (the consumer can be down or slow), in speed (absorbs bursts) and in scale (add consumers independently).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 558 68\" width=\"558\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A queue absorbs a burst so the worker is never overwhelmed\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 34 L310 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 34 L310 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M400 34 L456 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M400 34 L456 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Web server</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Queue</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Worker</text><rect x=\"456\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"501\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Database</text></svg><figcaption>A queue absorbs a burst so the worker is never overwhelmed</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A sale causes 5,000 orders/s for 60 s, while the email service handles 500/s. Without a queue, 4,500 requests/s fail or time out. With a queue the backlog grows by 4,500/s x 60 s = 270,000 messages (at 1 KB, 270 MB) and drains in about 540 s once traffic falls. The user got an instant \"order placed\".</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber, Swiggy and Zomato use queues/streams between order, dispatch and notification services. Amazon SQS processes enormous volumes of work items; Shopify uses Kafka widely.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A kitchen order rail: waiters pin tickets and move on; the chef cooks as fast as possible.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using a queue for a flow the user needs an immediate result from (needs sync response, or a status poll).</li>\n<li>Not saying what happens when the queue is full or the consumer is down.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"queue-vs-log-the-core-difference","title":"Queue vs log: the core difference","html":"<p><strong>A traditional queue deletes a message once it is consumed. A log keeps messages for a set time and consumers just track a position (offset).</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Queue (SQS, RabbitMQ):</strong> message goes to one consumer, is acknowledged, then removed. Good for \"do this job once\". Replaying means re-publishing.</li>\n<li><strong>Log (Kafka, Kinesis, Pulsar):</strong> an append-only ordered file. Many independent consumers read the same data at their own offsets. Replay is just resetting the offset.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 426.4 192\" width=\"426.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Queue: consumed and gone. Log: kept, each reader has an offset\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Producer</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Queue</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"105\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Log</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"359.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">One consumer</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"359.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Reader A</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"136\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"359.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Reader B</text></svg><figcaption>Queue: consumed and gone. Log: kept, each reader has an offset</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> A queue is simpler for task distribution. A log is best when several systems want the same events (search indexing, analytics, cache invalidation) or you need replay after a bug. Moving a system from queue to log later is painful because consumers' ack semantics differ: nearly a one-way door.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> LinkedIn built Kafka because many systems needed the same activity stream. Banks use RabbitMQ/IBM MQ for transactional work items.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A queue is a pile of letters that you throw away after reading. A log is a diary on a shelf that anyone can read from any page.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Calling Kafka \"just a faster queue\". Retention and replay change how you design.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that with a log, a slow consumer does not delete anything; it just lags.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"sqs-and-rabbitmq-in-practice","title":"SQS and RabbitMQ in practice","html":"<p><strong>SQS is a managed, almost infinitely scalable queue; RabbitMQ is a feature-rich broker you run (or rent).</strong></p>\n<p><strong>SQS:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard queue: nearly unlimited throughput, at-least-once delivery, best-effort ordering (duplicates and reordering happen).</li>\n<li>FIFO queue: strict order per <code>MessageGroupId</code>, exactly-once processing within a 5-minute dedup window using <code>MessageDeduplicationId</code>; throughput limited (about 300 msg/s per API action without batching, 3,000 with batching; higher with high-throughput mode; confirm current quotas).</li>\n<li><strong>Visibility timeout</strong> (default 30 s): after a consumer receives a message it is hidden; if not deleted in time, it reappears and is processed again. Max message size 256 KB (check docs). Dead-letter queue via a <code>maxReceiveCount</code> redrive policy.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>RabbitMQ:</strong> producers publish to an <strong>exchange</strong> (direct, topic, fanout, headers) which routes by binding to <strong>queues</strong>. Consumers ack manually; unacked messages are redelivered. Features: priorities, TTLs, delayed messages (plugin), per-message routing, quorum queues for replication. Throughput is tens of thousands msg/s per node, below Kafka for bulk streaming.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 614.4 130\" width=\"614.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"RabbitMQ routes through an exchange to queues\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Publisher</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Exchange</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Billing queue</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Email queue</text><rect x=\"477.6\" y=\"43\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"540\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Billing worker</text></svg><figcaption>RabbitMQ routes through an exchange to queues</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"RedrivePolicy\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"deadLetterTargetArn\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"arn:aws:sqs:...:orders-dlq\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"maxReceiveCount\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">5</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> },</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"VisibilityTimeout\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">60</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A video-transcoding job takes up to 4 minutes. If the SQS visibility timeout is 30 s, the message reappears while worker 1 is still busy and worker 2 starts the same job. Fix: set the timeout above the max job time (say 300 s) or extend it with a heartbeat.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Many AWS-based systems use SQS plus Lambda; RabbitMQ is common in enterprise integration and task systems (Celery commonly sits on it).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> SQS is a post office box you do not maintain; RabbitMQ is a sorting room with labelled slots you configure.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Visibility timeout shorter than processing time, causing duplicates.</li>\n<li>Assuming SQS Standard keeps order.</li>\n<li>Forgetting a DLQ, so a poison message loops forever.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"kafka-basics-topics-partitions-consumer-groups","title":"Kafka basics: topics, partitions, consumer groups","html":"<p><strong>A Kafka topic is split into partitions; each partition is an ordered, append-only log. A consumer group shares a topic: each partition is read by exactly one consumer in the group.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Parallelism = number of partitions.</strong> 12 partitions means at most 12 active consumers per group. A 13th sits idle.</li>\n<li><strong>Different groups are independent</strong> and each gets every message (this is how pub/sub works on Kafka).</li>\n<li>When consumers join or leave, a <strong>rebalance</strong> reassigns partitions; processing pauses for a moment (cooperative rebalancing in newer clients reduces this).</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 425.2 192\" width=\"425.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Each partition goes to one consumer in a group\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 34 L317.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 34 L317.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 96 L317.2 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 158 L317.2 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 158 L317.2 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Producer</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Partition 0</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Partition 1</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Partition 2</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"365.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer 1</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"105\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"365.2\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer 2</text></svg><figcaption>Each partition goes to one consumer in a group</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A topic of 6 partitions with 3 consumers: each gets 2 partitions. Add 3 more consumers: each gets 1. Add a 7th: it stays idle. If you need more throughput than 6 consumers give, you must add partitions (which changes key-to-partition mapping for new messages).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> LinkedIn (origin), Uber (trip events, dispatch), Netflix (data pipeline, Keystone), Swiggy and Flipkart event buses.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A multi-lane road where each lane has one toll booth (consumer in the group); another company's convoy (another group) can drive the whole road independently.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>More consumers than partitions does not speed things up.</li>\n<li>Believing the broker tracks which consumer processed what; the group stores offsets per partition.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"ordering-guarantees","title":"Ordering guarantees","html":"<p><strong>Kafka orders messages only within a single partition. Across partitions there is no global order.</strong> To keep the order for one entity (an order ID, a user), use that entity as the <strong>message key</strong>: <code>partition = hash(key) mod numPartitions</code>, so all its events land on the same partition.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Producer config for ordering with retries: <code>enable.idempotence=true</code> (also <code>max.in.flight.requests.per.connection&#x3C;=5</code>) so a retry cannot reorder or duplicate.</li>\n<li>Consumers must process a partition sequentially. Handing messages to a thread pool destroys order unless you shard by key.</li>\n<li>SQS FIFO orders per <code>MessageGroupId</code>. RabbitMQ orders per queue per single consumer; multiple consumers or requeues break it.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 598.8 68\" width=\"598.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Same key always goes to the same partition, so order is kept\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M281.6 34 L337.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M281.6 34 L337.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M440.8 34 L496.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M440.8 34 L496.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Order events</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Hash of key</text><rect x=\"337.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"389.20000000000005\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Partition 3</text><rect x=\"496.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"541.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumer</text></svg><figcaption>Same key always goes to the same partition, so order is kept</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choosing the key is nearly a one-way door: changing partition count remaps keys, and per-key order can be violated during the change. Pick a key with high cardinality and even spread; <code>country</code> as a key makes hot partitions.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Events for order 42: <code>created</code>, <code>paid</code>, <code>shipped</code>. Key = order ID keeps them in order. With random keys, <code>shipped</code> can be processed before <code>paid</code> by another consumer.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Banks key by account ID; Uber keys trip events by trip ID.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> All pages of one document go through one scanner in order; different documents can use different scanners.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Promising total ordering across a topic.</li>\n<li>Increasing partitions \"to scale\" without thinking about key remapping.</li>\n<li>Retries without idempotence causing reordering.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"when-to-use-which","title":"When to use which","html":"<p><strong>Pick by the job, not by the brand.</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Need</th>\n<th>Pick</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Simple background jobs on AWS, no ops</td>\n<td>SQS (+DLQ)</td>\n<td>Managed, scales, cheap</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Complex routing, priorities, per-message TTL</td>\n<td>RabbitMQ</td>\n<td>Exchanges and bindings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Many consumers need same events, replay, high throughput</td>\n<td>Kafka</td>\n<td>Log, retention, partitions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Streaming analytics, event sourcing</td>\n<td>Kafka / Kinesis</td>\n<td>Ordered log</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Very low volume, simple</td>\n<td>DB table or Redis list</td>\n<td>Do not over-build</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 554.8 130\" width=\"554.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Decision shortcut\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M354.8 34 L410.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M354.8 34 L410.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M354.8 96 L410.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M354.8 96 L410.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Workload</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"256.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Task distribution</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"256.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Event stream with replay</text><rect x=\"410.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"476.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SQS or RabbitMQ</text><rect x=\"410.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"476.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka</text></svg><figcaption>Decision shortcut</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> E-commerce: \"send receipt email\" (one consumer, retry, DLQ) fits SQS. \"Order placed\" event that billing, inventory, search, analytics and fraud all read, and which you may replay after a fraud-model bug, fits Kafka.</p>\n<p><strong>Operational cost.</strong> Kafka needs expertise (brokers, partitions, ISR tuning) or a managed service (MSK, Confluent Cloud); SQS is nearly zero ops. Cost of mistake: moving later is a migration project.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Many companies run both: Kafka as the event backbone, SQS/Rabbit for task queues.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A pickup truck for errands (SQS) versus a freight train system with timetables (Kafka).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Defaulting to Kafka for 10 messages per second.</li>\n<li>Using a queue as a database or for data you must query.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Queues decouple time, speed and scale; always size backlog growth and drain time.</li>\n<li>Queue deletes on consume; log retains and lets many groups replay by offset.</li>\n<li>SQS: visibility timeout, DLQ, Standard (unordered, at-least-once) vs FIFO (ordered per group). RabbitMQ: exchanges, bindings, acks.</li>\n<li>Kafka: partitions give parallelism and per-partition order; one consumer per partition per group.</li>\n<li>Order requires a key; partition count changes remap keys.</li>\n<li>Choose by workload: tasks to SQS/Rabbit, shared replayable events to Kafka.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}